From 16455d96008b9e8dae3c3e694e1c3280f272fcba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:49:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Record format and fixed record size for host imports (PCSI
 kits)

Imported files could only be Stream_LF (ods2 COPY) or carry a bare
rtype (ods2_put), always with RSIZE = MRS = 512 and no record
attributes. OpenVMS PCSI kit files are sequential files of fixed
8192-byte records; a Stream_LF or fixed-512 copy of the same bytes is
not a kit to PRODUCT, so a kit disk couldn't be prepared with ods2v2
alone.

Library: ods2_create_file_attrs() takes the record format, record
attributes (carriage control, BLK), record size and MRS, checked by
ods2_check_record_attrs() before anything is allocated:
- UDF, FIX and the stream formats only: VAR and VFC records start
  with a byte count on disk that host bytes don't have;
- a fixed record size is even, 2..32766, MRS equals it (as on VMS's
  own fixed files: INDEXF.SYS is FIX, RSIZE = MRS = 512), and the
  content is a whole number of records. Odd sizes are refused rather
  than written without the pad byte RMS puts after each odd record;
- valid RAT bits, at most one carriage control.
ods2_create_file() is unchanged.

ods2 COPY: /ATTRIBUTES on the command word, in SET FILE/ATTRIBUTES
syntax - COPY/ATTRIBUTES=(RFM:FIX,MRS:8192) kit.pcsi [KITS]KIT.PCSI;
RFM, MRS, LRL, RAT, VMS-style abbreviations. Not on the arguments,
since host paths contain '/'. Plain COPY is still Stream_LF.

ods2_put: optional record size and record attributes after rtype
(ods2_put disk kit.pcsi KITS KIT.PCSI 1 8192), all validated - a bad
rtype number was previously written as given. A fixed-record import
that isn't whole records is now refused instead of written malformed.

Tests: ods2_record_attrs_selftest (validation matrix; FIX 8192 header
and EOF; FIX 512 matching VMS's INDEXF.SYS; other formats; refusal
allocates nothing; legacy call unchanged) and cli_record_attrs_check.sh
(COPY/ATTRIBUTES and ods2_put variants, headers read back with
ods2_dump_header, refusals exit 1 and create nothing).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018ZqVjHFvXKcJm8prtYVbsY
